  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "H+rb1oW+/SgusTo8zgFd22EGHxk=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:22.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "`ISyncManager.add` is the single entry point for attaching a remote drive. It persists the remote record, creates its channel through the channel factory, and calls `channel.init()`:\n\n```typescript\nadd(\n  name: string,\n  collectionId: DriveCollectionId,\n  channelConfig: ChannelConfig,\n  filter?: RemoteFilter,\n  options?: RemoteOptions,\n  id?: string,\n): Promise<Remote>;\n```\n\n- `name` is the unique key across the manager. Reusing one throws ``Remote with name '${name}' already exists``.\n- `collectionId` identifies the drive; build it with `DriveCollectionId.forDrive(driveId, branch?)` (branch defaults to `\"main\"`).\n- `filter` defaults to `{ documentId: [], scope: [], branch: \"\" }` \u2014 empty arrays and an empty branch string all mean \"no restriction\".\n- `options` defaults to `{ sinceTimestampUtcMs: \"0\" }`, i.e. sync from the start of history.\n- `id` defaults to a generated UUID.\n\nThe important behavior is the failure path: **if `channel.init()` throws, `add` rolls the remote back out of both the in-memory map and storage, then rethrows the original error.** There is no half-registered remote to clean up. Calling `add` after `shutdown()` throws `\"SyncManager is shutdown and cannot add remotes\"`.\n\nConnect's `addRemoteDrive(url, driveId?, options?)` helper shows the canonical call. It reads `window.ph.reactorClient` and the sync manager, fetches `{ id, graphqlEndpoint }` from the URL, dedupes against `sync.list()`, then:\n\n```typescript\nawait sync.add(\n  crypto.randomUUID(),                 // name\n  DriveCollectionId.forDrive(driveId),\n  { type: \"gql\", parameters: { url: driveInfo.graphqlEndpoint } },\n  undefined,                           // filter -> no restriction\n  options?.pollBehavior ? { pollBehavior: options.pollBehavior } : undefined,\n);\n```\n\nNote that Connect passes a random UUID as the name \u2014 the name is an internal handle, not a label. To remove a drive, find every remote whose `meta.collectionId.equals(...)` and call `sync.remove(remote.meta.name)`. Config validation is eager: a `\"gql\"` config missing `url` throws at `add` time, as does any optional parameter with the wrong type.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/01-Reactor/04-Synchronization.md (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:22.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:22.000Z"
    }
  },
